Found it. The autoplay is in `SoundtrackProvider.tsx`. Here's the mechanism:

**File:** `apps/interface/src/features/Soundtrack/components/SoundtrackProvider.tsx`

**Lines 184-193** — `isPlaying` initializes from `localStorage`:
```ts
const [isPlaying, setIsPlayingState] = useState(() => {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return false;
  try {
    const stored = localStorage.getItem(PLAYING_STORAGE_KEY);
    return stored === 'true';  // <-- If user was playing before, auto-resumes on load
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
});
```

When `isPlaying` starts as `true`, the **useEffect at line 296-349** immediately loads a track and calls `audio.play()`.

**Fix:** Always initialize `isPlaying` to `false` so music never auto-starts on page load. Users can still manually start it via the UI button.

